// KDE Wayland, run "kscreen-doctor -o" in console to ID your displays
//
kscreen-doctor // followed by a space separated list of commands
output.DP-1.mode.1920x1080@120 // set output resolution and refresh rate
output.DP-1.colorPowerTradeoff.preferAccuracy // potentially significant performance hit from color correction
output.DP-1.colorPowerTradeoff.preferEfficiency // minimal performance hit from color correction
output.DP-1.iccprofile.$HOME/icc_current.icc // load this icc profile; I use a link to my active ICC profile
output.DP-1.iccprofile."" // leave blank to use no profile and allow direct scan out.

verify KDE Wayland direct scanout by opening "kwin debug console" enabling effect "showcompositing" and closing the debug window/console.
the red "compositing" overlay in the top right disappears when direct scanout is active. leaving the debug window open requires compositing.
color management and desktop effects can prevent direct scanout and degrade performance, especially with preferAccuracy/"Prefer Color Accuracy"
enabled, even without a color profile loaded. KWIN_DRM_USE_MODIFIERS=1 seems to reduce perf impact somewhat.

